00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:07.050
know if we could actually see his

00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:09.390
face and a vat of coffee beans, but

00:10:09.390 --> 00:10:10.650
we don't know who the hell he is.

00:10:11.295 --> 00:10:12.075
What are you doing in there?

00:10:12.075 --> 00:10:13.425
I'm just trying to find the character.

00:10:13.425 --> 00:10:14.705
I'm all in for Dunkin'.

00:10:17.335 --> 00:10:18.675
(*click sound).
Now, the one thing I do like

00:10:18.675 --> 00:10:20.505
that they do is the opponents

00:10:20.505 --> 00:10:22.005
are wearing a green uniform.

00:10:22.065 --> 00:10:23.385
They can't put Starbucks

00:10:23.685 --> 00:10:24.885
on their commercial or they

00:10:24.885 --> 00:10:26.145
get sued to high heaven.

00:10:26.385 --> 00:10:26.885
Right?

00:10:26.985 --> 00:10:28.755
But they have done a good job of making

00:10:28.755 --> 00:10:30.555
it clear that it is Dunkin' versus

00:10:30.555 --> 00:10:33.075
Starbucks and living in a town where the

00:10:33.075 --> 00:10:34.785
Starbucks and the Dunkin are literally

00:10:34.815 --> 00:10:36.195
across the street from each other.

00:10:36.395 --> 00:10:38.105
This they have done at least

00:10:38.105 --> 00:10:39.935
slightly well, but I'll tell

00:10:39.935 --> 00:10:41.375
you as this scene progresses,

00:10:41.405 --> 00:10:42.095
Get roasted!

00:10:42.185 --> 00:10:43.715
like a dark seasonal roast with

00:10:43.715 --> 00:10:45.515
coriander and slight balsamic drizzle.

00:10:45.545 --> 00:10:47.285
Sounds like what's in my garbage disposal.

00:10:47.855 --> 00:10:48.665
That was the funniest

00:10:48.665 --> 00:10:49.475
line in the whole thing.

00:10:49.655 --> 00:10:50.465
See you coach.

00:10:50.525 --> 00:10:51.845
How much to wait a half hour to get

00:10:51.845 --> 00:10:53.045
my name spelled wrong on the cup?

00:10:53.405 --> 00:10:54.454
Nobody wants a gold milk.

00:10:54.454 --> 00:10:55.805
Double half calf salt milk cap.

00:10:55.835 --> 00:10:56.795
You could just brew it.

00:10:56.795 --> 00:10:57.905
It's beans and water.

00:10:57.965 --> 00:10:58.715
Oh damn.

00:11:00.020 --> 00:11:01.250
Listen, Dunkin's for all of you.

00:11:01.670 --> 00:11:02.120
That's it.

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:04.040
Duncan is for all of you, that is the

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:05.600
whole point of the commercial, right?

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:07.340
It took him forever to get to the

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:09.560
idea that Dunkin is for all of you,

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:11.210
and the only way they made that

00:11:11.210 --> 00:11:12.950
point was essentially Casey Affleck

00:11:12.950 --> 00:11:14.960
said, nobody wants your coffee.

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:16.370
It's just beans and water.

00:11:16.430 --> 00:11:18.650
Essentially, the whole commercial

00:11:18.950 --> 00:11:21.980
comes down to the idea that coffee is

00:11:21.980 --> 00:11:24.860
nothing but beans and water, therefore.

00:11:25.545 --> 00:11:26.895
You should go to Dunkin' Donuts.

00:11:26.925 --> 00:11:27.704
That is it.

00:11:28.185 --> 00:11:31.185
They undermine the idea of what coffee

00:11:31.185 --> 00:11:34.214
is, beans and water, nothing more.

00:11:34.605 --> 00:11:37.225
And therefore, because of that, Dunkin'

00:11:37.245 --> 00:11:40.694
Donuts is the best because, because we

00:11:40.694 --> 00:11:42.824
have Bill Belichick and Casey Affleck

00:11:42.824 --> 00:11:44.985
and Ben Affleck and some people, I still

00:11:44.985 --> 00:11:46.365
can't figure out who the hell they are.

00:11:46.605 --> 00:11:48.584
That's not a great message.

00:11:48.885 --> 00:11:50.355
When your company's message

00:11:50.385 --> 00:11:51.944
about the product you make is.

00:11:52.215 --> 00:11:53.235
It's kind of nothing.

00:11:53.265 --> 00:11:54.495
It's just beans and water.

00:11:54.645 --> 00:11:55.575
That doesn't make me think,

00:11:55.575 --> 00:11:56.655
well, hell, I gotta go get the

00:11:56.655 --> 00:11:57.825
Dunkin' Donuts, beans and water.

00:11:57.885 --> 00:11:59.385
They throw a whole bunch of things

00:11:59.385 --> 00:12:01.125
on the screen and they hope that

00:12:01.125 --> 00:12:02.925
something resonates with you.

00:12:03.285 --> 00:12:07.005
Jeep presents a clear, clean, obvious

00:12:07.005 --> 00:12:09.555
message from a single spokesperson who

00:12:09.555 --> 00:12:12.075
everyone knows and who everyone trusts.

00:12:12.615 --> 00:12:14.145
This commercial, this Dunkin

00:12:14.145 --> 00:12:15.735
Donuts commercial, it is a mistake.

00:12:16.185 --> 00:12:18.285
It fails to take account for audience.

00:12:18.915 --> 00:12:19.905
That is the difference between

00:12:19.905 --> 00:12:20.955
these two commercials, and that is

00:12:20.955 --> 00:12:22.305
what we must do as storytellers.

00:12:22.485 --> 00:12:24.675
First and foremost, before you open your

00:12:24.675 --> 00:12:26.505
mouth or put your pen to the page or your

00:12:26.505 --> 00:12:29.145
fingers to the keys, the first thing you

00:12:29.145 --> 00:12:32.625
ask yourself is who is your audience?

00:12:33.105 --> 00:12:34.935
And then you craft a message

00:12:35.115 --> 00:12:36.555
that that audience will listen

00:12:36.555 --> 00:12:38.505
to, believe and understand.

00:12:38.895 --> 00:12:40.035
Jeep did it brilliantly.

00:12:40.495 --> 00:12:41.565
Dunkin' Donuts failed.

